Z||000016||frontal lobe||11-30-2000||06:53 PM||||A great appeal about the 2.8L Fiero is grunt, grunt, grunt.  With 165 to 170 ft-lbs of torque, it really pulls well from a stop.  HP is 135-140, which for the wt. of the car is pretty good.  Wt. is around 2750 pounds.||||reg||1
Z||000017||PearlBlueSoul||11-30-2000||09:48 PM||||I'll vouch for that one on pull!  damn, I love it.  hehe.  1FSTM6's Asstek 3.4l v6 fiero is a BLAST to ride in.  very nimble too I might add, but i'd have to run with him on a twisty road to see that one.  hehe....that and get some bigger wheels.  I'm running on 185/60s right now so I'm hurtin for less sidewall flex.<BR><P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
